{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Of Pitru.</b> Like this table (פטורא) upon which everyone sets coins before him — so all the kings send their letters to him. And according to the plain sense of Scripture, it is the name of the place (ibid.)." "<b>Land of the children of his people.</b> Balak's — he was from there. And he would prophesy and say to him: You are destined to rule. And if you say: Why did the Holy One, blessed be He, cause His Shechinah to rest upon a wicked nation? — so that the nations would not have an opening to say, 'If we had had prophets, we would have returned to the good.' He established prophets for them, and they breached the fence of the world: at first they were fenced off in their cities, and this one gave them advice to abandon themselves to harlotry." "<b>To call him.</b> The calling was his own and for his benefit — he would stipulate for him much money." "<b>A people has come out of Egypt.</b> And if you say: What does it harm you?" "<b>Behold, it has covered the eye of the land.</b> Sihon and Og, who were guarding us — they came against them and killed them." "<b>And he dwelt among the nations.</b> It is written deficient — they are close to wiping me out, as in ״כִּי אֲמִילַם״ (Psalms 118) — this is its midrash (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:11.418531865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}